Gene silencing comprises a suite of biotechnological approaches that selectively suppress the expression of specific genes at either the transcriptional or post‑transcriptional level. The three core modalities-RNAi, ASOs and CRISPR‑mediated transcriptional repression-offer complementary mechanisms for knocking down disease‑causing proteins, while each presents its own set of delivery, safety and regulatory considerations.

